        "original_id": "77ed2d70-b99b-5b24-bb69-9528434ca8d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Newark, Nottinghamshire, England\n- Organizations: UK Parliament, Conservative Party, Standards Committee\n- People: Robert Jenrick, Patrick Mercer\n- Events: 2001 general election, May 2013 resignation of party whip, April 2014 resignation, 5 June 2014 by-election\n\nFacts:\n- Newark is a UK Parliament constituency in Nottinghamshire, England.\n- Patrick Mercer was elected as the Conservative MP for Newark in the 2001 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer resigned the Conservative Party parliamentary whip in May 2013 following questions about paid advocacy.\n- Patrick Mercer then sat as an Independent MP for Newark until his resignation at the end of April 2014.\n- The Standards Committee suspended Patrick Mercer for six months for a sustained and pervasive breach of the House's rules.\n- Robert Jenrick of the Conservative Party won the Newark by-election on 5 June 2014.\n- Robert Jenrick has represented Newark since winning the by-election triggered by Patrick Mercer’s April 2014 resignation.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f2169925-35ae-50a0-b700-90fedb9c162b",
        "text": "Page: Newark (UK Parliament constituency). Sentence: Newark is a constituency in Nottinghamshire, England.\nPage: Newark (UK Parliament constituency). Sentence: It is currently represented by Robert Jenrick of the Conservative Party, who won the seat in a by-election on 5 June 2014, following the resignation of Patrick Mercer in April 2014.\nPage: Patrick Mercer. Sentence: He was elected as a Conservative in the 2001 general election, until resigning the party's parliamentary whip in May 2013 following questions surrounding paid advocacy, and was an Independent MP representing the constituency of Newark in Parliament until his resignation at the end of April 2014 after the Standards Committee suspended him for six months for \"sustained and pervasive breach of the house's rules\".",
